<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds lacked any clear direction in thin volume, with absence of liquidity pushing the spread wider with the Spanish 10-year cash.</p>
<p>Traders did not expect the mood to change ahead of the three-day Christmas break.</p>
<p>&quot;For this year, the accounts have been closed,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't see any relevance to the price movements at this time of the year because they are not based on any significant liquidity,&quot; said another.</p>
<p>--Fernanda Pargana, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
